<codeline lineno="8"><highlight class="comment"><sp/>*<sp/>The<sp/>`TopJets`<sp/>class,<sp/>implemented<sp/>in<sp/>Cython,<sp/>is<sp/>a<sp/>specialized<sp/>selection<sp/>template<sp/>within<sp/>the<sp/>AnalysisG<sp/>framework,<sp/>designed<sp/>for<sp/>comprehensive<sp/>analysis<sp/>of<sp/>top-tagged<sp/>jets<sp/>and<sp/>their<sp/>underlying<sp/>parton<sp/>associations<sp/>in<sp/>Monte<sp/>Carlo<sp/>16<sp/>(MC16)<sp/>events.<sp/>It<sp/>inherits<sp/>from<sp/>the<sp/>generic<sp/>`SelectionTemplate`<sp/>class,<sp/>extending<sp/>its<sp/>functionalities<sp/>to<sp/>extract<sp/>and<sp/>organize<sp/>detailed<sp/>information<sp/>about<sp/>jet<sp/>masses,<sp/>parton<sp/>contributions<sp/>to<sp/>jets,<sp/>and<sp/>the<sp/>relationship<sp/>between<sp/>jets<sp/>and<sp/>top<sp/>quarks.<sp/>This<sp/>class<sp/>facilitates<sp/>a<sp/>high-performance<sp/>extraction<sp/>and<sp/>structuring<sp/>of<sp/>top-jet<sp/>data<sp/>for<sp/>further<sp/>physics<sp/>analysis.</highlight></codeline>
